Fix the orca Docker image so ``[pack]`` command stages with ``docker = true`` actually run: the traversal path to the uv-managed Python (``/home/estampo/.local/share/uv/python/…``) now has every parent directory a+rx, including ``/home/estampo`` itself. Previously the #641 chmod stopped one level too deep, so the non-root ``estampo`` user could not reach the Python interpreter and ``bambox repack`` crashed with ``Could not find platform independent libraries``. This matches how ``Dockerfile.cura`` already handles ``/root``.
